== Maintenance surfaces ==

These are software-generated operational reports, not ordinary content pages:

* [[Special:AllPages]] — enumerate pages by namespace;
* [[Special:Categories]] — categories with members;
* [[Special:UncategorizedPages]] — pages without category tags;
* [[Special:UncategorizedTemplates]] — templates without category tags;
* [[Special:UnusedTemplates]] — templates not currently transcluded;
* [[Special:WantedCategories]] — categories with members but no created category page;
* [[Special:UnusedCategories]] — created categories with no members;
* [[Special:BrokenRedirects]] and [[Special:DoubleRedirects]] — migration/redirect hygiene.

== V1 → V2 template/category migration ==

<pre>
archive title + raw source + revision/history
→ identify transclusions/category membership
→ compare duplicate/variant implementations
→ preserve unique writing and behavior
→ decide KEEP / REWRITE / MERGE / REDIRECT / RETIRE
→ implement V2
→ run Special-page maintenance checks
</pre>

A missing category page does not mean the category is unused: MediaWiki can have members in a category whose editable Category: page has never been created. Likewise, an unused template is not automatically disposable.

== Release checks ==

Before a V2 deployment is considered clean:

# review all Template namespace pages against the V1 template archive;
# review [[Special:UncategorizedTemplates]];
# review [[Special:UnusedTemplates]] deliberately, not destructively;
# review [[Special:Categories]] and [[Special:WantedCategories]];
# review [[Special:UncategorizedPages]];
# verify that every V2 category/template has documentation or an explicit reason not to;
# verify redirects and transclusions after renames.

